content.text:
verdict: findings
draft_version_seen: 3
checks:
  - {claim: "Summary 1", question: "Do SFIA 9, IASA, Open CA, AWS, Microsoft, Google define/certify the title as stated, and do TOGAF (secondhand) and Gartner (secondhand) scope it narrowly while SFIA-6 and SAFe scope it broadly?", source_reopened: "sfia-online.org; opengroup.org; iasa-global.github.io; docs.aws.amazon.com; learn.microsoft.com; cloud.google.com; grahamberrisford.com; en.wikipedia.org; framework.scaledagile.com/solution-architect", result: pass, notes: "All confirmed: Google title is 'Professional Cloud Architect' with no 'Solutions Architect' on page; Berrisford quotes TOGAF 'typically applies to a single project or project release'; Wikipedia gives Gartner 'architectural description of a specific solution'; SAFe abstract 'shared technical and architectural vision for a Solution Train'; SFIA-6 'across multiple projects or initiatives'."}
  - {claim: "Summary 2", question: "Do Open CA, IASA and SFIA say the quoted words about technical vision, delivery value and business outcomes?", source_reopened: "opengroup.org; iasa-global.github.io; sfia-online.org", result: pass, notes: "All three quotes verbatim in primary sources; 'broader than lead-architect' is the report's comparison, not sourced, and reads as such."}
  - {claim: "Summary 3", question: "Does any source assign product-wide stack ownership to the title, and do Queensland, IASA-EA, Hohpe and the Advice Process say what is quoted?", source_reopened: "forgov.qld.gov.au; iasa-global.github.io; martinfowler.com/articles/architect-elevator.html; martinfowler.com/articles/scaling-architecture-conversationally.html", result: pass, notes: "Queensland 'Solutions architects decide which technologies to use' verbatim; IASA tool-selection sentence sits under Enterprise Architect; Hohpe bounds passage verbatim; Advice Process rule verbatim; reconciliation correctly labeled as judgment/medium."}
  - {claim: "Summary 4", question: "Does the DDD source say boundaries are the architect's job, does the SAFe summary say 'define the systems, subsystems and interfaces', and are these secondary/abstract-only?", source_reopened: "avanscoperta.it/en/context-mapping/; scrum-master.org", result: pass, notes: "Both quotes verbatim; 'define[s]' bracket edit is honest; medium label matches scheme (no primary opened in full)."}
  - {claim: "Summary 5", question: "Is Pettersson's decision-rights sentence a real quote, the argument paraphrase fair, and SAFe's peer-leader framing visible?", source_reopened: "pettersson.dev; framework.scaledagile.com/product-management/", result: pass, notes: "'When both roles understand their decision rights, conflict becomes collaboration.' verbatim; SAFe abstract names PM and System Architect among 'leaders of the Agile Release Train'."}
  - {claim: "Summary 6", question: "Are the Fowler, Thoughtworks and TOGAF Phase G claims accurately quoted/paraphrased and is 'high' defensible?", source_reopened: "martinfowler.com/ieeeSoftware/whoNeedsArchitect.pdf (PDF unreadable); martinfowler.com/architecture/; thoughtworks.com (both); conexiam.com", result: unverified, notes: "Fowler PDF would not extract for me; 'inversely proportional' wording corroborated only by secondary snippets; Thoughtworks Adopt/Trial and ARB sentence verbatim; Conexiam three options and 'the choice of action belongs to a Stakeholder' verbatim."}
  - {claim: "F1", question: "Are the SFIA level texts, Open CA, IASA deliverables, TOGAF-secondhand scope and Wikipedia skills-framework sentence quoted accurately?", source_reopened: "sfia-online.org; opengroup.org; iasa-global.github.io; grahamberrisford.com; en.wikipedia.org", result: pass, notes: "SFIA quotes verbatim but truncated without ellipsis (L6 continues 'within a significant area' / 'ensuring consistency with agreed requirements'); IASA page does list 'optimized solution designs', so 'solution designs' is now verifiable and should not stay UNVERIFIED; 'impact analyses' remains unfound (page says 'impact on the overall topology')."}
  - {claim: "F2", question: "Do Queensland, AWS, Microsoft, IASA, Hohpe and Harmel-Law say the quoted words, and is the two-level reconciliation marked as judgment?", source_reopened: "forgov.qld.gov.au; docs.aws.amazon.com; learn.microsoft.com; iasa-global.github.io; martinfowler.com (elevator; scaling-architecture-conversationally)", result: pass, notes: "All verbatim; AWS quote truncated ('...and future projected needs') without ellipsis; Advice Process 'anyone' is lowercase in source; judgment correctly labeled medium."}
  - {claim: "F3", question: "Do the Avanscoperta pages, scrum-master.org, Mind the Product and continuous-architecture.org say what is quoted, including capacity for enablement work?", source_reopened: "avanscoperta.it (both); scrum-master.org; mindtheproduct.com; continuous-architecture.org; framework.scaledagile.com/system-architect", result: pass, notes: "All quotes verbatim except 'manages capacity for enablement work', which I could not find on scrum-master.org or the SAFe abstract — mark that clause paraphrase/unverified; 'partnership' is among the listed relationship kinds."}
  - {claim: "F4", question: "Are the Pettersson heading and lists, ondata definitions, SAFe PM abstract and Lawson/Mind the Product failure-mode quotes accurate?", source_reopened: "pettersson.dev; ondata.blog; framework.scaledagile.com/product-management/; linkedin.com (Lawson); mindtheproduct.com", result: fail, notes: "All verbatim except ondata: source reads 'agree on the role description upfront' — draft drops 'the' inside quotation marks; PM quote 'define the product' and 'represents the client (user) voice' confirmed; Lawson 'setting yourself up for failure' verbatim; MtP 'blocked by other teams' verbatim."}
  - {claim: "F5", question: "Are the Fowler/Johnson attribution, Thoughtworks rings and ARB sentence, the ARB RACI reading, and the Conexiam Phase G paraphrase accurate?", source_reopened: "martinfowler.com/architecture/ (Johnson attribution confirmed); whoNeedsArchitect.pdf unreadable; thoughtworks.com (both); theartofcto.com; conexiam.com", result: unverified, notes: "Johnson attribution confirmed on martinfowler.com/architecture; RACI (Engineer R/A for proposal, ARB C; CTO A for approve/reject) confirmed; Conexiam confirmed; the Fowler 'inversely proportional' quote rests on an unreadable primary from this context."}
confidence_labels: "F5 and summary 6 'high' are defensible only for the governance instruments (two Thoughtworks primaries plus Conexiam secondary agree); the Fowler decision-count claim rests on a primary I could not read, which the scheme scores low — either cite a readable copy of the Fowler text or split the label (high on governance, medium/low on Fowler). All other labels defensible; no confidence/likelihood combinations found."
top_changes: ["Fix ondata quote in F4 to 'agree on the role description upfront'", "Move 'solution designs' out of UNVERIFIED in F1 (IASA page lists 'optimized solution designs'); keep 'impact analyses' UNVERIFIED", "Mark 'manages capacity for enablement work' in F3 as unverified/paraphrase (not on scrum-master.org or the SAFe abstract)", "Add ellipses where SFIA level-6 and AWS quotes are truncated mid-sentence", "Re-source or split-label the Fowler claim in F5/summary 6 (PDF unreadable to a fresh context; Johnson attribution verifiable on martinfowler.com/architecture)"]
